    {
      "id": "zh-u01-l02",
      "titulo": "Initials and finals",
      "explicacao": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A Chinese syllable has three parts: an initial (the consonant at the start), a final (the rest) and a tone. 妈 mā = m + a + 1st tone."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Most initials sound close to Portuguese. These are the ones that surprise Portuguese speakers:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabela",
          "cabecalho": [
            "Pinyin",
            "How it sounds",
            "Example"
          ],
          "linhas": [
            [
              "b, d, g",
              "like a soft Portuguese p, t, k (no puff of air)",
              "八 bā (eight)"
            ],
            [
              "p, t, k",
              "p, t, k with a strong puff of air",
              "他 tā (he)"
            ],
            [
              "h",
              "like the rough r in \"carro\"",
              "好 hǎo (good)"
            ],
            [
              "j",
              "like \"dj\" in Brazilian \"dia\", but softer",
              "九 jiǔ (nine)"
            ],
            [
              "q",
              "like \"tch\" in \"tchau\", with a puff of air",
              "七 qī (seven)"
            ],
            [
              "x",
              "like \"x\" in \"xícara\", with the lips spread",
              "谢 xiè (thank)"
            ],
            [
              "zh, ch, sh",
              "like \"dj\", \"tch\" and \"x\" with the tongue curled back",
              "是 shì (to be)"
            ],
            [
              "z, c",
              "like \"dz\" and \"ts\" (c has a puff of air)",
              "菜 cài (dish)"
            ],
            [
              "r",
              "between the English r and the Portuguese j",
              "人 rén (person)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabela",
          "cabecalho": [
            "Final",
            "How it sounds",
            "Example"
          ],
          "linhas": [
            [
              "i after z, c, s",
              "a buzzing sound, not an i",
              "四 sì (four)"
            ],
            [
              "i after zh, ch, sh, r",
              "a buzzing sound with the tongue curled back",
              "是 shì (to be)"
            ],
            [
              "ü",
              "say i with rounded lips, like the French u",
              "女 nǚ (female)"
            ],
            [
              "e",
              "a sound from the back of the throat, between \"â\" and \"ê\"",
              "喝 hē (to drink)"
            ],
            [
              "-n and -ng",
              "-n ends at the teeth; -ng ends in the throat, as in English \"song\"",
              "人 rén, 冷 lěng"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "dica",
          "texto": "After j, q, x and y, the letter u is always ü, even without the dots: 去 qù sounds like \"tchü\"."
        }
      ],
      "exemplos": [
        {
          "frase": "八",
          "pinyin": "bā",
          "en": "eight",
          "pt": "oito"
        },
        {
          "frase": "他",
          "pinyin": "tā",
          "en": "he",
          "pt": "ele"
        },
        {
          "frase": "七",
